  <section>
    <h2>Overview</h2>
    <p>High Road is one of two medical cannabis dispensaries operating in Gray, Maine, alongside Token Cannabis Co. on Lewiston Road. The store sits at 21 Portland Road, Suite 7 — a small commercial plaza on the main Route 26 corridor through Gray. The MDG Gray dispensary guide credits the operator with a perfect 5.0-star rating from 113 Weedmaps reviews, making High Road one of the higher-rated medical dispensaries in Cumberland County by review volume.</p>
    <p>The store was founded by Robert Thibodeau and Eric Dudevoir, who per the MDG guide have built a strong reputation around patient care and product quality. The two-store Gray medical infrastructure (High Road plus Token Cannabis Co.) has established Gray as a functional medical-cannabis destination on the Portland-Auburn commuter corridor, even though the town has not yet attracted any adult-use (recreational) operators.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Location and Access</h2>
    <p><strong>Address:</strong> 21 Portland Road, Suite 7, Gray, ME 04039<br>
    <strong>Phone:</strong> (207) 391-9420<br>
    <strong>Email:</strong> 207highroad@gmail.com<br>
    <strong>Hours (per MDG Gray guide):</strong> Open daily 10am onwards.</p>
    <p>Gray is a Cumberland County town of roughly 8,200 residents positioned on the I-95 / Route 26 corridor between Portland and Auburn. Portland Road is the main commercial strip through town — the same corridor that anchors much of Gray's retail activity. The suite-7 location is accessible from Route 26 and is convenient for commuters traveling between Portland and the Sebago Lakes region. The store's proximity to I-95 (Gray is roughly equidistant between Portland and Auburn) gives High Road a wider effective service area than the town's resident population would suggest.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>License and Product Information</h2>
    <p>Per the MDG Gray dispensary guide, High Road is registered as a Maine medical cannabis dispensary. As of publication, the operator's menu categories, pricing, and cultivation sources are not separately documented in the MDG operator registry. The MDG guide does note that Gray has opted in to recreational cannabis but has not yet attracted an adult-use operator — a status that affects whether High Road's medical patients are also able to make adult-use purchases on-site.</p>
    <p class="pending-verification"><strong>Pending verification:</strong> Field-level details that have not yet been confirmed against the operator's own primary source include: (a) detailed product categories (flower / edibles / concentrates / vapes / topicals), (b) closing time, (c) delivery availability, (d) any current promotional or discount programs for veterans, seniors, or first-time patients. Last research date: <strong>2026-07-08</strong>. Call (207) 391-9420 or email 207highroad@gmail.com for current details.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Service Area</h2>
    <p>From the Portland Road storefront, High Road serves the central Cumberland County / Portland-Auburn corridor:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Gray</strong> (in town) — 5 min</li>
      <li><strong>Windham</strong> — 10 min south</li>
      <li><strong>Raymond</strong> — 15 min northwest (via Route 302)</li>
      <li><strong>Cumberland</strong> — 10 min southeast</li>
      <li><strong>North Yarmouth</strong> — 10 min east</li>
      <li><strong>New Gloucester</strong> — 12 min north</li>
      <li><strong>Portland</strong> — 20 min south via I-95</li>
      <li><strong>Auburn</strong> — 25 min north via I-95</li>
    </ul>
    <p>For adult-use customers who do not have a Maine MMMP card, the nearest recreational dispensaries are in Naples, Raymond (Eclipse Cannabis Company), or Portland — each 15–25 minutes from Gray. For other medical patients in towns without a local dispensary (Standish, Sebago, Otisfield, Poland), High Road is a reasonable drive from much of the western Cumberland / Sebago Lakes region.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How to Verify Before You Go</h2>
    <p>Operator details — hours, license status, product menu, and accepted payment — can change without notice. To avoid a wasted trip, verify directly before visiting:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Phone:</strong> (207) 391-9420</li>
      <li><strong>Email:</strong> 207highroad@gmail.com</li>
      <li><strong>Weedmaps listing:</strong> <a href="https://weedmaps.com/dispensaries/high-road">weedmaps.com/dispensaries/high-road</a> (verify the active URL with the operator)</li>
      <li><strong>Gray guide:</strong> <a href="/guides/gray-dispensary-guide">Gray Dispensary Guide</a> — town-level overview of all Gray dispensaries including Token Cannabis Co.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Medical patients: bring your Maine MMMP card and a valid photo ID. Out-of-state patients with a valid card from a Maine reciprocity state should call ahead to confirm acceptance. Adult-use (21+) customers should confirm that the operator is licensed for recreational transactions before visiting, as the MDG Gray guide's current data shows High Road as medical-only.</p>
  </section>

